    "q-81216": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81216",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "$$\nV=\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V$ and an **orthonormal** basis $B$ of $V,$ given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $|a|+|b|+|c|?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{5\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot 0+10\\cdot 3}{{4}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize each vector to get an orthonormal basis:\n\n- ${u}_{1}=\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- ${u}_{2}=\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{4}^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3\\sqrt{41}}{41} \\\\ -\\frac{4\\sqrt{41}}{41} \\\\ \\frac{4\\sqrt{41}}{41}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{u}_{1},{u}_{2}\\}=\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3\\sqrt{41}}{41} \\\\ -\\frac{4\\sqrt{41}}{41} \\\\ \\frac{4\\sqrt{41}}{41}\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is an orthonormal basis of $V.$\n\nFinally, $a=-\\frac{3\\sqrt{41}}{41},$ $b=-\\frac{4\\sqrt{41}}{41},$ $c=\\frac{4\\sqrt{41}}{41}$ and  \n\n$$\n|a|+|b|+|c|=|-\\frac{3\\sqrt{41}}{41}|+|-\\frac{4\\sqrt{41}}{41}|+|\\frac{4\\sqrt{41}}{41}|=\\frac{11\\sqrt{41}}{41}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-81216-a",
