    "q-86852": {
      "dom_id": "step-q86852",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "$$\nV=\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{11} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{11} \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{11}}{11}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V$ and an **orthonormal** basis $B$ of $V,$ given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $|a|+|b|+|c|?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{2\\cdot (-1)+7\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 3}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize each vector to get an orthonormal basis:\n\n- ${u}_{1}=\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-\\sqrt{11}}{11} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{11} \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{11}}{11}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- ${u}_{2}=\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3\\sqrt{46}}{46} \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{46}}{23} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{46}}{46}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{u}_{1},{u}_{2}\\}=\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-\\sqrt{11}}{11} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{11} \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{11}}{11}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3\\sqrt{46}}{46} \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{46}}{23} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{46}}{46}\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is an orthonormal basis of $V.$\n\nFinally, $a=\\frac{3\\sqrt{46}}{46},$ $b=\\frac{3\\sqrt{46}}{23},$ $c=-\\frac{\\sqrt{46}}{46}$ and  \n\n$$\n|a|+|b|+|c|=|\\frac{3\\sqrt{46}}{46}|+|\\frac{3\\sqrt{46}}{23}|+|-\\frac{\\sqrt{46}}{46}|=\\frac{5\\sqrt{46}}{23}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-86852-a",
